+# Consulted Broadcom sources
+
+The sources below were consulted using live network requests.
+
+- “Upgrade Sequence and Related Issues for VMware Cloud Foundation and vSphere Foundation 9.1,” Broadcom Knowledge Base article 440630, https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/440630/upgrade-sequence-and-related-issues-for.html — accessed 2026-08-13; informed the Operations-first sequence, mandatory Management Services and License Server deployment, management-network IP pool, and subsequent lifecycle-managed component upgrades.
+- “Unified VCF Product Releases & Versioning,” Broadcom Knowledge Base article 410435, https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/410435/unified-vcf-product-releases-versioning.html — accessed 2026-08-13; informed the unified 9.1.0.0 component target convention used by the greenfield design.
+- “Required Component Binaries for VCF 9.1 upgrade,” Broadcom Knowledge Base article 425089, https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/425089/required-component-binaries-for-vcf-91.html — accessed 2026-08-13; informed the staged-binary gates for primary-instance Fleet Lifecycle and SDDC Lifecycle deployment.
+- “Broadcom Product Interoperability and Compatibility,” https://interopmatrix.broadcom.com/Interoperability — accessed 2026-08-13; informed the vCenter, ESXi, vSAN, NSX, and witness combination at the selected target release and the source-to-target upgrade paths.
